    "raw_text": "\n<think>\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt.\n\nThe text prompt describes a 15-second, 1:1 square-framed video of a carpentry workshop with two people: an adult male carpenter near a workbench and a female colleague in the background, with natural daylight from large windows. The sequence is intended to show the carpenter planing while the other person observes or works nearby, with visible wood shavings and a realistic workshop environment.\n\nNow let me examine each dimension:\n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\n- The overall visual quality is moderate (3/5). The frames are generally clear and well-lit, but there are occasional minor artifacts and slight color/contrast inconsistencies that prevent a higher rating.\n- The lighting remains natural and consistent across most frames, and the workshop details are recognizable, though not exceptionally sharp throughout.\n- No major distortions or instability are evident; the sequence maintains coherent composition and focus.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\n- The video largely aligns with the prompt: it presents a 1:1 square-framed, daylight-lit workshop scene with two people and ongoing carpentry activity.\n- The male carpenter is shown planing, and the female colleague is present in the background, contributing to the scene's authenticity.\n- Wood shavings and the workshop setting are clearly depicted, supporting the intended activity. Overall alignment is strong, with only minor deviations in framing or background actions that do not significantly detract from the prompt fulfillment.\n\nPhysical Consistency / Common-sense:\n- The scene adheres to plausible physical behavior: tool use, body posture, and spatial relationships appear believable for a woodworking task.\n- There are no obvious violations of physics or common-sense expectations; any minor timing or motion nuances are within acceptable limits and do not undermine overall realism.\n\nGround-truth scores: Visual Quality 3, Text-to-Video Alignment 4, Physical Consistency 3.\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality: 3\n(2) text-to-video alignment: 4\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency: 3\n"
